---
// Anatomy of a run id.
---

<figure class="fig">
            <div style="border: 1px solid var(--rule); background: var(--card); padding: 20px; display: grid; gap: 22px; min-width: 0">
              <div style="overflow-x: auto; min-width: 0">
                <div style="display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(5, auto); justify-content: start; row-gap: 8px; font: 500 clamp(1rem, 2.4vw, 1.5rem)/1.2 var(--mono)">
                  <span style="padding-bottom: 6px; border-bottom: 2px solid var(--ink)">gend</span>
                  <span style="color: var(--rule-3); padding-bottom: 6px">__</span>
                  <span style="padding-bottom: 6px; border-bottom: 2px solid var(--ink)">hidf_video</span>
                  <span style="color: var(--rule-3); padding-bottom: 6px">__</span>
                  <span style="padding-bottom: 6px; border-bottom: 2px solid var(--accent); color: var(--accent-ink); justify-self: start">3f9a1c2e</span>
                  <span style="font: 400 12px/1.4 var(--mono); color: var(--muted); padding-right: 8px">model id</span>
                  <span></span>
                  <span style="font: 400 12px/1.4 var(--mono); color: var(--muted); padding-right: 8px">evalset id</span>
                  <span></span>
                  <span style="font: 400 12px/1.4 var(--mono); color: var(--accent-ink)">8 hex over every input</span>
                </div>
              </div>
              <div style="display: grid; grid-template-columns: var(--f-two); gap: 16px 32px">
                <div style="display: grid; gap: 6px; align-content: start">
                  <span style="font: 500 11.5px/1.4 var(--mono); color: var(--muted)">The hex covers</span>
                  <ul style="margin: 0; padding-left: 1.1em; font-size: 0.9rem; line-height: 1.5; display: grid; gap: 2px"><li>the upstream commit</li><li>every weight hash, the face detector's included</li><li>the model, evalset and eval configs</li><li>the preprocessing mode</li></ul>
                </div>
                <div style="display: grid; gap: 10px; align-content: start; font-size: 0.9rem; line-height: 1.45">
                  <div style="display: grid; grid-template-columns: 22px minmax(0, 1fr); gap: 8px"><span style="font: 500 15px/1.3 var(--mono)">=</span><span>Same inputs, same folder: the run resumes.</span></div>
                  <div style="display: grid; grid-template-columns: 22px minmax(0, 1fr); gap: 8px"><span style="font: 500 15px/1.3 var(--mono)">≠</span><span>Any input changes: a new folder, so settings never mix.</span></div>
                  <div style="display: grid; grid-template-columns: 22px minmax(0, 1fr); gap: 8px; color: var(--muted)"><span style="font: 500 15px/1.3 var(--mono)">·</span><span>Not in the id: repo commit and device, recorded per session in <code>run.json</code>.</span></div>
                </div>
              </div>
            </div>
            <figcaption><strong>Anatomy of a run id.</strong> Face caches follow the same pattern, <code>&lt;detector&gt;__&lt;8 hex&gt;</code>, with the settings spelled out in <code>spec.json</code>. The hex shown is an example.</figcaption>
          </figure>
